  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6655726",
      "title": "Understanding the Role of AppModule and Component Declaration",
      "lectureOrder": 338,
      "videoOrder": 316,
      "sourceHash": "03a73a738c44d7c17b5020859af9003d3c091b64ab091bba7eeea9b542df6044",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.7,
          "end": 3.78,
          "en": "-: In the last lecture",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.78,
          "end": 7.56,
          "en": "we created our own component, the server component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.56,
          "end": 11.28,
          "en": "It's almost ready to be used, but to use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.28,
          "end": 14.7,
          "en": "we need to change something about our app module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.7,
          "end": 16.74,
          "en": "What is a app module?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.74,
          "end": 20.22,
          "en": "Angular users components to build webpages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.22,
          "end": 25.14,
          "en": "and users modules to basically bundle different pieces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.14,
          "end": 29.49,
          "en": "for example, components of your app into packages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.49,
          "end": 32.13,
          "en": "Now this is kind of an advanced feature, but later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.13,
          "end": 35.58,
          "en": "in the course I will have a whole section about modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.58,
          "end": 37.47,
          "en": "For the majority of this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.47,
          "end": 40.68,
          "en": "we will only use the app module, which is absolutely fine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.68,
          "end": 43.41,
          "en": "for a lot of projects only in bigger projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.41,
          "end": 44.79,
          "en": "you might think about splitting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.79,
          "end": 47.49,
          "en": "up your app into multiple opt modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.49,
          "end": 49.47,
          "en": "But what does this app module do?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.47,
          "end": 51.48,
          "en": "What is a module then?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.48,
          "end": 55.02,
          "en": "Well, it's a, as I said, bundle of functionalities",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.02,
          "end": 58.89,
          "en": "of our app and it basically gives angled information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.89,
          "end": 62.43,
          "en": "which features does my app have and use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.43,
          "end": 65.52,
          "en": "As you can see, it also is just a empty TypeScript class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.52,
          "end": 67.32,
          "en": "like our component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.32,
          "end": 70.86,
          "en": "And as the component, we transform it into something else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.86,
          "end": 74.88,
          "en": "by adding a decorator here it's the NG module decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.88,
          "end": 78.273,
          "en": "which is also imported from @Angular/core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.2,
          "end": 82.59,
          "en": "Now, in there we see four properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.59,
          "end": 83.82,
          "en": "We set up on the object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.82,
          "end": 87.96000000000001,
          "en": "we passed to NG module, declarations, imports, providers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.96000000000001,
          "end": 89.31,
          "en": "and bootstrap.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.31,
          "end": 90.93,
          "en": "We had a look at Bootstrap.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.93,
          "end": 93.84,
          "en": "This was responsible for telling Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.84,
          "end": 96.47999999999999,
          "en": "Hey, which component should you be aware of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.47999999999999,
          "end": 99.15,
          "en": "at the point of time the whole application starts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.15,
          "end": 101.43,
          "en": "so which component should you basically recognize",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.43,
          "end": 102.99000000000001,
          "en": "in the index html file?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.99000000000001,
          "end": 105.27000000000001,
          "en": "And that was the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 105.27000000000001,
          "end": 106.8,
          "en": "Now, I already mentioned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 106.8,
          "end": 109.44,
          "en": "that we won't add any more component selectors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 109.44,
          "end": 110.94,
          "en": "to the index html file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 110.94,
          "end": 113.03999999999999,
          "en": "That's just not how it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 113.03999999999999,
          "end": 116.22,
          "en": "Therefore, we won't touch the bootstrap array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 116.22,
          "end": 119.58,
          "en": "Still, we added a new component to Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 119.58,
          "end": 123.09,
          "en": "and this new component now has to be registered here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 123.09,
          "end": 125.19,
          "en": "in the module so that Angular knows",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 125.19,
          "end": 128.22,
          "en": "that this component exists because, and this is important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 128.22,
          "end": 133.22,
          "en": "by default, Angular will not scan all your files here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 133.56,
          "end": 138.56,
          "en": "So if you don't tell it that the server component exists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 139.14,
          "end": 143.37,
          "en": "it doesn't know it, just creating the file is not enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 143.37,
          "end": 146.82,
          "en": "That is why we have to register it here in the NG module to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 146.82,
          "end": 147.9,
          "en": "tell Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 147.9,
          "end": 151.47,
          "en": "Hey, part of this module, and therefore right here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 151.47,
          "end": 154.41,
          "en": "of our whole app since we only have this module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 154.41,
          "end": 156.78,
          "en": "is this server component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 156.78,
          "end": 161.61,
          "en": "We do register new components in this declarations array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.61,
          "end": 164.91,
          "en": "We already registered the app component here because even",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 164.91,
          "end": 167.31,
          "en": "though it's all used in Bootstrap, it also is a part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 167.31,
          "end": 168.54,
          "en": "of our app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 168.54,
          "end": 173.54,
          "en": "Now we also need to add the server component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 173.67000000000002,
          "end": 175.92000000000002,
          "en": "Adding it like this is not enough though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 175.92000000000002,
          "end": 178.29,
          "en": "because now Angular would kind of know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 178.29,
          "end": 179.82,
          "en": "that this is part of the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 179.82,
          "end": 182.85,
          "en": "but type script wouldn't know where to find this type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 182.85,
          "end": 184.74,
          "en": "where to find the server component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 184.74,
          "end": 189.24,
          "en": "So when we try to bundle our code, we would get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 189.24,
          "end": 190.77,
          "en": "which you can actually see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 190.77,
          "end": 194.31,
          "en": "if you save this triggering the recompilation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 194.31,
          "end": 197.19,
          "en": "You see that we get an error in the terminal down there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 197.19,
          "end": 200.1,
          "en": "that it can't find server component because,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 200.1,
          "end": 202.07999999999998,
          "en": "and this is not Angular, this is type script.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 202.07999999999998,
          "end": 203.82,
          "en": "It doesn't know where this file is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 203.82,
          "end": 205.89,
          "en": "where to find this class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 205.89,
          "end": 208.11,
          "en": "So we need to add import at the top",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 208.11,
          "end": 210.72,
          "en": "manually pointing to this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 210.72,
          "end": 212.88,
          "en": "So we add server component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 212.88,
          "end": 217.87,
          "en": "as a import from ./server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 218.73,
          "end": 223.41,
          "en": "and then here in the server component, and you omit the .ts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 223.41,
          "end": 226.07999999999998,
          "en": "you don't add .ts to your import,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 226.07999999999998,
          "end": 227.79,
          "en": "it's just server.component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 227.79,
          "end": 229.92000000000002,
          "en": "So the file name without the extension,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 229.92000000000002,
          "end": 231.93,
          "en": "the extension is added by Webpack",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 231.93,
          "end": 234.99,
          "en": "which bundles our project automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 234.99,
          "end": 236.94,
          "en": "So with this, and it's just so important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 236.94,
          "end": 237.9,
          "en": "this is not Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 237.9,
          "end": 239.49,
          "en": "This is a types good feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 239.49,
          "end": 242.19,
          "en": "Now TypeScript knows where to find this, therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 242.19,
          "end": 243.69,
          "en": "everything can be bundled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 243.69,
          "end": 246.78,
          "en": "So therefore now Angular when it runs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 246.78,
          "end": 249.21,
          "en": "knows that we have a server component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 249.21,
          "end": 251.1,
          "en": "and that it is part of our app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 251.1,
          "end": 254.55,
          "en": "And with this we can now finally use our component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 254.55,
          "end": 256.11,
          "en": "We will do this in the next lecture",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 256.11,
          "end": 258.51,
          "en": "but maybe you are also wondering what imports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 258.51,
          "end": 261.48,
          "en": "and providers does here in the app module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 261.48,
          "end": 265.26,
          "en": "I'll come back to providers later in the services section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 265.26,
          "end": 269.1,
          "en": "Imports simply allows us to add some other modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 269.1,
          "end": 271.38,
          "en": "to this module because I told you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 271.38,
          "end": 273.57,
          "en": "you can split up your app into multiple modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 273.57,
          "end": 276.33,
          "en": "and then you can import this modules to basically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 276.33,
          "end": 277.95,
          "en": "make this module a bit leaner",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 277.95,
          "end": 280.59000000000003,
          "en": "and outsource some stuff into an module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 280.59000000000003,
          "end": 283.47,
          "en": "Now, I told you that we are only going to use one module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 283.47,
          "end": 285.33,
          "en": "So what are we importing here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 285.33,
          "end": 287.19,
          "en": "Some modules built into Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 287.19,
          "end": 290.43,
          "en": "because Angular itself is split up into modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 290.43,
          "end": 292.17,
          "en": "So the browser module, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 292.17,
          "end": 294.99,
          "en": "gives us all the base functionality we need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 294.99,
          "end": 297.96,
          "en": "to start our app and forms an HDP module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 297.96,
          "end": 299.34000000000003,
          "en": "That is something I'll come back to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 299.34000000000003,
          "end": 302.1,
          "en": "in (indistinct) or HTP section of the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 302.1,
          "end": 305.58,
          "en": "So with this, the basics about this module should be clear.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 305.58,
          "end": 308.58,
          "en": "Again, we'll dive deeper into this later in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 308.58,
          "end": 311.16,
          "en": "we also register our own component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 311.16,
          "end": 313.413,
          "en": "Let's now use it in the next lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
